text:
Jules Park: Heads-up: the new next-eval-starter using LlamaIndex intermittently fails in prod with 401s during onboarding. Followed README, set REDWOOD_API_KEY. SSR pages blow up. Anyone seen auth rotation issues with the JS SDK? cc @Ibrahim

Ibrahim Noor: Could be key rotation. Are you using a module-scoped client? If so, serverless cold starts can reuse a stale instance.

Jules Park: Yep, simple API handler below used in starter:
```js
// pages/api/query.js
import { createClient } from '@redwood/inference-js'
const client = createClient(process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY)
export default async (req, res) => {
  const out = await client.embed({ model: 'redwood/mini', input: req.body.text })
  res.json(out)
}
```

Hana Rivera: JS SDK doesn't yet implement the rotation-watch parity that Python added. Workaround: instantiate client inside handler or catch 401 + check x-rw-exp and retry once after re-creating client. We'll add a note to the starter README.

CI Bot: triggered workflow/devex-e2e on branch fix/instantiate-per-request :runner:

Ibrahim Noor: I'll open a small PR to add a retry on 401 when x-rw-exp indicates imminent rotation and add an e2e sim. Assigning DEVEX-4210.

Jules Park: Thanks — added a short repro to the repo under docs/auth-rotation.md and verified staging after CI. ISR pages stable now. :thumbsup:
